From d44daa9007f44b03e99577811c1ee0776b612aad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Jackson <70459+jjackson@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:22:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Labs mode: signing v2 (timestamp, method, path, token
 hash, HQ host, body)

A v1 labs signature covers only the body, so a captured request can be replayed
later, to another endpoint, with another worker's token or against another HQ
server. v2 signs a canonical block - v2, METHOD, path, X-Labs-Timestamp,
sha256hex(token), X-Labs-HQ-Host - followed by the body (or multipart JSON
part), and the timestamp must be within 300 s.

LabsAuthFilter: when X-Labs-Signature-V2 is present only v2 is checked (a v1
header alongside cannot downgrade it); otherwise v1 is accepted only while
formplayer.labs.allowV1 (LABS_ALLOW_V1, default true) so labs can switch over
without a deploy-order dependency. CSRF is skipped for any labs request, not
only ones with the v1 header. Tests include a pinned vector computed outside
Java, replay outside the window, and path, token, host and body swaps.
